---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Background, interests and tools of Lucas Rodriguez, junior data scientist in Montevideo.">
  <div class="wrap grid gap-12 pt-10 md:pt-16 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,4fr)] lg:gap-20">
    <div>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-[2.6rem] leading-[1.05] font-[400] tracking-[-0.015em] [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_72] md:text-5xl">About</h1>
      <div class="prose-case mt-8">
        <p>
          I'm studying statistics at Universidad de la República and data science and business analytics at the University of
          London, in parallel. The two programmes pull in useful directions: one towards inference and getting the assumptions
          right, the other towards building things that run.
        </p>
        <p>
          What I care about most is the part of the work that rarely shows in a chart: knowing what a zero in a column really
          means, choosing a metric that matches the decision, and leaving an analysis that someone else can rerun and question.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside coursework I'm interested in probabilistic forecasting and prediction markets, public data about Uruguay, and
          tools that make university courses easier to follow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="space-y-10 font-sans lg:pt-24">
      <section aria-labelledby="edu">
        <h2 id="edu" class="text-sm font-semibold">Education</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-4">
          {
            site.education.map((e) => (
              <li>
                <p class="font-medium">{e.degree}</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-2">{e.school}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-2">{e.note}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="tools">
        <h2 id="tools" class="text-sm font-semibold">Tools I use</h2>
        <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3">
          {
            site.tools.map((g) => (
              <div>
                <dt class="text-sm text-ink-2">{g.group}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-0.5">{g.items.join(', ')}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="lang">
        <h2 id="lang" class="text-sm font-semibold">Languages</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Spanish (native), English.</p>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
